#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:116
msgid ""
"Path parameters are always required because they are part of the URL itself. "
"You can only get a \"missing\" path parameter when the same handler is "
"registered against :ref:`multiple paths <usage/routing/parameters:path "
"parameters>` (e.g. ``[\"/items\", \"/items/{id:int}\"]``), in which case the "
"handler-side default fills in for the path without the slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:124
msgid "Parameter types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:127
msgid "Path parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:129
msgid ""
"Path :term:`parameters <parameter>` are declared as part of the ``path`` "
"component of the URL using the syntax ``{param_name:param_type}``. The "
"handler function receives the value via a parameter of the same name, "
"declared with :data:`~.params.FromPath`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:134
msgid "Defining a path parameter in a route handler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:134
msgid ""
"import dataclasses\n"
"\n"
"from litestar import Litestar, get\n"
"from litestar.params import FromPath\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@dataclasses.dataclass\n"
"class User:\n"
"    id: int\n"
"    name: str\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"USER_DB = {1: User(id=1, name=\"John Doe\")}\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@get(\"/user/{user_id:int}\", sync_to_thread=False)\n"
"def get_user(user_id: FromPath[int]) -> User:\n"
"    return USER_DB[user_id]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"app = Litestar(route_handlers=[get_user])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:137
msgid "There are two components to declaring a path parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:139
msgid ""
"In the :class:`@get() <.handlers.get>` :term:`decorator`, the path component "
"declares both the parameter's name (``user_id``) and type (:class:`int`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:141
msgid ""
"In the handler signature, ``user_id`` is declared as :data:`FromPath[int] <."
"params.FromPath>`, which tells Litestar to inject the matching path value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:145
msgid "Two characteristics are unique to path parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:147
msgid ""
"The URL slot defines the structurally required type via the ``:type`` suffix "
"(see :ref:`usage/routing/parameters:supported path parameter types` below). "
"Litestar coerces the captured string into this type before passing it to the "
"handler, and the handler-side type annotation can request a further coercion "
"(see :ref:`usage/routing/parameters:type coercion`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:152
msgid ""
"Path parameters cannot be declared on application :ref:`layers <usage/"
"applications:layered architecture>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:156
msgid ""
"You only need to declare the path :term:`parameter` in the function "
"signature if the handler actually uses it. If the path parameter is part of "
"the path but the function does not consume it, you can omit it from the "
"signature; it will still be validated and added to the OpenAPI schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:163
msgid "Supported path parameter types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:165
msgid "The following types are supported in the ``{name:type}`` slot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:167
msgid "``date``: Accepts date strings and time stamps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:168
msgid "``datetime``: Accepts date-time strings and time stamps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:169
msgid "``decimal``: Accepts decimal values and floats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:170
msgid ":class:`float`: Accepts ints and floats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:171
msgid ":class:`int`: Accepts ints and floats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:172
msgid ":class:`path`: Accepts valid POSIX paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:173
msgid ":class:`str`: Accepts all string values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:174
msgid ""
"``time``: Accepts time strings with optional timezone compatible with "
"standard (Pydantic/Msgspec) datetime formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:175
msgid ""
"``timedelta``: Accepts duration strings compatible with the standard "
"(Pydantic/Msgspec) timedelta formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:176
msgid "``uuid``: Accepts all uuid values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:179
msgid "Query parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../usage/routing/parameters.rst:181
